  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nFor words with Latin characters case insensitive Server Side Search by keywords works well: we can send two messages with `hello` and `HeLLo`content, and find both of them via `hello`, `HeLLo` and even `HELLO` search string.\r\n\r\nBut when we try same thing with non-Latin words, for example - Russian word \"Привет\" - search becomes case sensitive!\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Send to room two messages with English words `hello` and `HeLLo`content.\r\n2. Make a search in this room via keyword \"HELLo\" - you will find both messages.\r\n3. Send to room two messages with Russian words `привет` and `приВЕТ`content.\r\n4. Make a search in this room via keyword \"Привет\" - you will find nothing!\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: matrix.org or any other homeserver with default PostgreSQL database settings.",
